      "text" : "Radicals - Square Roots"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960199999999986,
        664.07150000000001,
        296.0495228821685,
        11.955199999999991
      ],
      "text" : "Objective: Simplify expressions with square roots."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960199999999986,
        637.65954480000005,
        425.2195267980544,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "Square roots are the most common type of radical used. A square root “un-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960199999999986,
        623.0193448,
        226.47228840999998,
        13.298257699999908
      ],
      "text" : "squares” a number. For example, because 52"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        313.4402,
        623.0193448,
        196.69251174179846,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "= 25 we say the square root of 25 is 5."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960399999999964,
        608.25924480000003,
        178.73512623370252,
        22.047155199999906
      ],
      "text" : "The square root of 25 is written as"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        277.56092808970243,
        608.25924480000003,
        15.610886310297587,
        22.047155199999906
      ],
      "text" : "25 √ ."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960000000000008,
        581.85924480000006,
        425.2028208721664,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "World View Note: The radical sign, when first used was an R with a line"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960000000000022,
        567.21904480000001,
        425.20193290954251,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "through the tail, similar to our perscription symbol today. The R came from the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960000000000036,
        552.45924479999996,
        425.17279825446411,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "latin, “radix”, which can be translated as “source” or “foundation”. It wasn’t until"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960000000000036,
        537.81904479999992,
        425.15784547223041,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "the 1500s that our current symbol was first used in Germany (but even then it"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960000000000036,
        523.17924479999988,
        273.61278314347538,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "was just a check mark with no bar over the numbers!"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
